course: dictionary
lesson: 2493
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word dealer is a good example. «New cars travel to dealers on double-deck car transporter lorries.» Here a dealer is a business that buys and sells cars, because the cars travel to them.
explain: Ask yourself: what is the dealer doing in this sentence? If the words are about cards, the dealer hands the cards out. If the words are about buying and selling, the dealer sells things. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some dealers sell illegal drugs. A drug dealer breaks the law and may try to pull young people in. If anyone ever offers you drugs, say no, walk away, and tell a trusted adult straight away.
fact: A dealer is a person or business that buys and sells a particular kind of thing.
fact: Car dealers, art dealers and antique dealers each buy and sell things in their own area.
fact: In card games, the dealer is the person who hands out the cards.
fact: A drug dealer is a person who sells illegal drugs, which is against the law.
fact: «Dealers» is the plural of dealer: more than one dealer.
exercise: «New cars travel to dealers on double-deck car transporter lorries.» In this sentence, what is a dealer? | A driver of a lorry | A person who hands out cards | A part of a car engine | *A business that buys and sells cars
exercise: Sam says, «It's my turn to be the dealer.» In a card game, what does dealer mean? | A player who wins every hand | *The person who hands out the cards | A person who sells cars | A person who sells illegal drugs
exercise: Which word is the plural of dealer? | *dealers | dealing | dealership | dealt
test: Mia reads, «The antique dealer found an old clock at the sale.» What is an antique dealer? | A person who makes clocks | A player who hands out cards | *A person who buys and sells old, valuable things | A teacher who teaches history
test: What should you do if someone offers you drugs? | *Say no and tell a trusted adult | Hide it in your bag | Take one to look cool | Keep it secret from everyone
exam: Which meaning fits «Who is the dealer tonight?» at a card game? | A person who sells illegal drugs | *The person who hands out the cards | A person who buys and sells cars | A business that sells art
